<title>USA: First U.S. polls close in Indiana and Kentucky.</title>
<headline>First U.S. polls close in Indiana and Kentucky.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first polls in the U.S. election closed at 6 p.m. EST (2300 GMT) on Tuesday in the states of Indiana and Kentucky.</p>
<p>President Bill Clinton, a Democrat, won Kentucky in 1992. Indiana has voted for Republican presidents since 1940, except for 1964 when it was part of a national landslide victory for Democrat Lyndon Johnson.</p>
</text>
